/P 43 0 R
/T (The original draft included reaction equations for copper, silver and gold. Some of those equations are incomplete or chemically unbalanced, and the statement that a generic acid mixture will dissolve both gold and silver is too broad. In particular, nitric acid alone does not normally dissolve gold; gold dissolution generally requires an appropriate oxidising chloride system. Reaction equations should be verified and balanced for the exact reagent system before inclusion in a formal patent or laboratory document.)
/E (The original draft included reaction equations for copper, silver and gold. Some of those equations are incomplete or chemically unbalanced, and the statement that a generic acid mixture will dissolve both gold and silver is too broad. In particular, nitric acid alone does not normally dissolve gold; gold dissolution generally requires an appropriate oxidising chloride system. Reaction equations should be verified and balanced for the exact reagent system before inclusion in a formal patent or laboratory document.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
