549 0 obj
<<
/Title (The original draft included reaction equations for copper, silver and gold. Some of those equations are incomplete or chemically unbalanced, and the statement that a generic acid mixture will dissolve both gold and silver is too broad. In particular, nitric acid alone does not normally dissolve gold; gold dissolution generally requires an appropriate oxidising chloride system. Reaction equations should be verified and balanced for the exact reagent system before inclusion in a formal patent or laboratory document.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 531 0 R
>>
